-- Seeds the blog posts that the site already publishes, so the admin panel
-- opens on the real articles and the rendered pages are unchanged.
--
-- Text columns hold plain text, not markup: the renderer escapes on output.
-- body_html and FAQ answers are the exception and stay as authored HTML.
--
-- Guarded per slug rather than on the table being empty: the hosting platform
-- may apply these migrations itself, in which case the worker's migrator
-- replays them and an unguarded INSERT would duplicate every post.
INSERT INTO `blog_posts` (slug, status, position, seo_title, meta_description, og_image, banner_image, category, heading, published_label, author, body_html, faqs, card_title, card_excerpt, card_image)
SELECT 'top-beachside-wedding-venues-goa', 'published', 0, 'Beachside Wedding Venue in Goa: Top 7 Resorts & Costs', 'Beautiful photos won’t reveal how well a resort could work for a wedding. Compare the best beachside wedding venue in Goa by cost, guest capacity and location.', '/storage/blog/seo/MMTBP1ef1gqcO0RA8u90iEuccfl7M9K8PWvO9NPS.webp', '/storage/blogs/aCPvkbtbPXKRUgJINRFbo1aRqO71cvRnobu8nBqi.webp', 'Wedding Planning', 'Top Beachside Wedding Venues in Goa: Costs, Capacity & Locations', 'August 11, 2026', 'Viraaya Weddings Team', '<!--?xml encoding="UTF-8"--><p>You’ve probably already imagined it: pheras with the waves in the background and a cocktail hour overlooking the Arabian Sea as evening settles in. Goa’s blend of Portuguese-era charm, relaxed coastal living and luxury beachfront resorts is exactly what makes it one of India’s most sought-after <a href="/destination-wedding-in-goa"><strong>beach wedding destinations</strong></a><strong>.</strong> Then the planning starts. Suddenly you’re juggling fifteen browser tabs, three WhatsApp groups full of well-meaning advice and no clear way to tell which resort actually fits your guest list, budget or dates.</p><p>At Viraaya Weddings, we see this happen with couples every single week. The easiest way to cut through the overwhelm isn’t by looking at more venues, but by focusing on the right ones from the start. So before we dive into a list of properties, let’s get the filters right, because the “best” beachside wedding venue in Goa for an intimate 60-guest celebration is rarely the best choice for a wedding with 400 guests.</p><p> </p><h2 id="what-should-you-decide-before-shortlisting-a-venue">What Should You Decide Before Shortlisting a Venue?</h2><p>Three things shape this decision more than anything else, and getting clear on them first will save you weeks of back and forth:</p><p><strong>1. What’s your realistic guest count?</strong></p><p>Boutique properties are usually a great fit for celebrations with 50 to 150 guests. If your guest list is likely to cross 250, you’ll be better served by a larger resort designed to host weddings at that scale, such as Grand Hyatt Goa or Alila Diwa.</p><p><strong>2. North Goa or South Goa?</strong></p><p>Wedding venues in South Goa (Benaulim, Varca, Majorda, Cavelossim) are much calmer, offering a relaxed pace, ideal for couples who want the sea as a backdrop without the crowds. On the other hand, North Goa properties near Vagator lean toward a more vibrant vibe, closer to nightlife, and popular for a livelier sangeet or reception.</p><p><strong>3. How many functions are you planning?</strong></p><p>A beach wedding in Goa with four or five separate events (mehendi, sangeet, ceremony, reception) needs a property with enough distinct indoor and outdoor spaces to avoid overlap. This is worth confirming before you fall for a single beautiful lawn.</p><p>Once these three are locked in, comparing <strong>beach wedding venues in Goa</strong> becomes far more straightforward, especially in one of India’s most sought-after beach wedding destinations.</p><p> </p><h2 id="beachside-wedding-venues-in-goa-quick-comparison">Beachside Wedding Venues in Goa: Quick Comparison</h2><p>Use this comparison to quickly narrow down venues based on your guest count, location and wedding style:</p><figure class="table"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Venue</strong></td><td><strong>Location</strong></td><td><strong>Rooms</strong></td><td><strong>Residential Capacity</strong></td><td><strong>Best For</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Azaya Beach Resort</td><td>Benaulim, South Goa</td><td>114</td><td>Up to 250</td><td>Chic, mid-sized weddings</td></tr><tr><td>Caravela Beach Resort</td><td>Varca, South Goa</td><td>~200</td><td>Up to 420</td><td>Large multi-day weddings</td></tr><tr><td>Taj Exotica Resort &amp; Spa</td><td>Benaulim, South Goa</td><td>140</td><td>Up to 300</td><td>Classic luxury weddings</td></tr><tr><td>Grand Hyatt Goa</td><td>Bambolim</td><td>313</td><td>Up to 650</td><td>Large guest lists, on-site stay</td></tr><tr><td>W Goa</td><td>Vagator, North Goa</td><td>~150</td><td>Up to 320</td><td>Contemporary, party-forward weddings</td></tr><tr><td>Alila Diwa Goa</td><td>Majorda, South Goa</td><td>153</td><td>Up to 330</td><td>Very large, grand celebrations</td></tr><tr><td>Prainha Resort by the Sea</td><td>Cavelossim, South Goa</td><td>Boutique</td><td>Intimate</td><td>Small, private weddings</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><ol><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/azaya-beach-resort-goa"><strong>Azaya Beach Resort, Benaulim</strong></a><strong>: </strong>An Azaya Beach Resort Goa wedding suits couples who want private beach access without the scale of a mega-resort. Whitewashed, Portuguese-inspired architecture, multiple lawns and its own stretch of sand within the property.<br><br> </li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/caravela-beach-resort"><strong>Caravela Beach Resort, Varca</strong></a><strong>: </strong>Set along the white sands of Varca Beach, this 5-star beachfront resort features three banquet halls and five outdoor lawns for celebrations of different sizes. A Caravela Beach Resort Goa wedding cost typically depends on your guest count, room requirements and the event spaces you choose.<br><br> </li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/taj-exotica-resort-and-spa-goa"><strong>Taj Exotica Resort &amp; Spa, Benaulim</strong></a><strong>: </strong>Spread across 56 acres, with one of Goa’s largest pillarless ballrooms alongside expansive lawns, suited to both intimate and large-scale celebrations.<br><br> </li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/grand-hyatt-goa"><strong>Grand Hyatt Goa, Bambolim</strong></a><strong>: </strong>One of the few Goa wedding resorts genuinely built to host large weddings on a single campus, removing the headache of shuttling guests between properties.<br><br> </li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/w-goa"><strong>W Goa, Vagator</strong></a><strong>: </strong>For a younger, more experiential vibe, W Goa’s Rockpool and beachfront lawns lean contemporary and party-forward.<br><br> </li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/alila-diwa-goa"><strong>Alila Diwa Goa, Majorda</strong></a><strong>: </strong>Set amid paddy fields close to the coast, combining a soulful, understated setting with event spaces capable of hosting celebrations of up to around 1,200 guests.<br><br> </li><li><p><a href="/destination-wedding/goa/the-st-regis-goa-resort"><strong>The St. Regis Goa Resort, Cavelossim</strong></a><strong>: </strong>Set beside Mobor Beach, The St. Regis Goa Resort combines expansive lawns, lagoon-style landscapes and understated luxury, making it one of Goa’s most sought-after venues for premium destination weddings.</p><p> </p></li></ol><h2 id="what-does-a-beachside-wedding-venue-in-goa-cost">What Does a Beachside Wedding Venue in Goa Cost?</h2><p>After choosing the venue, the <a href="/destination-wedding-in-goa"><strong>cost of a destination wedding in Goa</strong></a><strong> </strong>is usually the next thing couples ask us about, especially when comparing India’s most popular beach wedding destinations. While your final budget depends on your guest count, travel dates and the kind of celebration you want to host, these ranges offer a practical starting point:</p><ul><li><strong>Boutique or mid-sized resorts (up to 150 guests):</strong> Around INR 50 lakhs to INR 1 Cr for a two-day celebration.</li><li><strong>Large beachfront resorts (200 to 400 guests):</strong> Around INR 1 Cr to INR 2.5 Cr for celebrations spread across two to three days.</li></ul><p>Please note that Goa wedding cost and Goa beach wedding cost figures vary with décor, room requirements and the scale of your celebration.</p><p><i>Prices and availability are subject to hotel policies, seasonality and demand. Final bookings are confirmed only after written hotel confirmation.</i></p><p> </p><h2 id="bringing-it-all-together">Bringing It All Together</h2><p>Once you’ve matched a venue to your guest count and region, it’s worth checking if that same property doubles as one of the better <strong>Goa pre-wedding locations</strong>, since many resort lawns and beachfront corners work just as well for a shoot as they do for the ceremony itself. It saves a separate booking and a separate briefing.</p><p>Shortlisting venues doesn’t have to mean chasing multiple hotels and juggling endless quotations. At <a href="/"><strong>Viraaya Weddings</strong></a>, we help you compare properties for destination weddings in Goa by bringing pricing and availability information together in one place, so choosing the right venue feels a lot more straightforward.</p><p><a href="/wedding-consultation"><strong>Book a consultation with Viraaya Weddings</strong></a> to find the right beachside wedding venue in Goa for the wedding you’ve always pictured.</p>', '[{"id": 34, "question": "How far in advance should I book a beachside wedding venue in Goa?", "answer": "<p>For a beachside wedding venue in Goa, it’s best to book 8 to 12 months in advance if you’re planning a wedding between October and February, because the most sought-after dates at popular resorts are often reserved first.</p>"}, {"id": 35, "question": "Is outside catering allowed at beach wedding venues in Goa?", "answer": "<p>Whether beach wedding venues in Goa allow outside catering depends on the property. Most luxury resorts prefer in-house catering, although some may permit external vendors for specific ceremonies, so it’s always worth confirming before you book.</p>"}, {"id": 36, "question": "Should I choose North Goa or South Goa for my wedding?", "answer": "<p>Deciding between North Goa and South Goa starts with the kind of celebration you want for yourselves and your guests. South Goa is known for quieter beachfront settings, while North Goa offers a livelier atmosphere. Your guest list, budget and preferred experience should guide the decision.</p>"}]', 'Top Beachside Wedding Venues in Goa: Costs, Capacity & Locations', 'You’ve probably already imagined it: pheras with the waves in the background and a cocktail hour overlooking the Arabian...', '/storage/blogs/aCPvkbtbPXKRUgJINRFbo1aRqO71cvRnobu8nBqi.webp'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `blog_posts` WHERE `slug` = 'top-beachside-wedding-venues-goa');
--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `blog_posts` (slug, status, position, seo_title, meta_description, og_image, banner_image, category, heading, published_label, author, body_html, faqs, card_title, card_excerpt, card_image)
SELECT 'top-destination-wedding-places-rajasthan', 'published', 1, 'Top 10 Destination Wedding Places in Rajasthan for Luxury Celebrations', 'Every third couple who walks into a conversation with us at Viraaya Weddings mentions Rajasthan before we even ask where they’re thinking of getting married....', '/storage/blogs/fMkxUPVWyH9i9g0VTTX0Mdfg2NFbGNAtDBhMhPTh.webp', '/storage/blogs/fMkxUPVWyH9i9g0VTTX0Mdfg2NFbGNAtDBhMhPTh.webp', 'Wedding Planning', 'Top 10 Destination Wedding Places in Rajasthan for Luxury Celebrations', 'August 07, 2026', 'Viraaya Weddings Team', '<!--?xml encoding="UTF-8"--><p>Every third couple who walks into a conversation with us at Viraaya Weddings mentions Rajasthan before we even ask where they’re thinking of getting married. Lately, it has become the default answer for anyone who wants their wedding to look like it belongs in a history book rather than a banquet hall.</p><p>At Viraaya Weddings, we’ve guided families through venue searches across Udaipur, Jaipur, Jodhpur and Jaisalmer, and one thing is clear: Rajasthan has no shortage of stunning wedding venues. The real difficulty arises when you have to narrow ten stunning hotels down to the one that actually fits your guest count, preferred dates and budget. So here’s a list of <strong>destination wedding places in Rajasthan</strong> that we get asked about most, along with what makes each one worth a closer look.</p><p> </p><h2 id="which-udaipur-palaces-suit-a-destination-wedding">Which Udaipur Palaces Suit a Destination Wedding?</h2><p>Udaipur is where most couples planning a destination wedding start looking, and it’s usually the city that ends up on the shortlist regardless of where the search began:</p><ul><li><a href="/destination-wedding/udaipur/taj-lake-palace-udaipur"><strong>Taj Lake Palace in Udaipur</strong></a> sits in the heart of Lake Pichola and is best known for an intimate palace wedding in Rajasthan. Its smaller scale is exactly what attracts couples looking for exclusivity over size.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/udaipur/the-oberoi-udaivilas-udaipur"><strong>The Oberoi Udaivilas</strong></a> offers sweeping lake views, private domed pavilions and a service standard that is hard to match anywhere else in the state.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/udaipur/the-leela-palace-udaipur"><strong>The Leela Palace Udaipur</strong></a><strong> </strong>strikes a lovely balance between grandeur and intimacy, with spacious lawns and elegant banquet spaces that comfortably accommodate both mid-sized and larger celebrations.</li></ul><p>At these properties, boutique weddings generally start from around INR 50 lakhs, while larger multi-day celebrations can range between INR 2 and 3 Cr, depending on your guest count, catering and overall wedding plans.</p><p>If you’re set on a lakeside setting, we’ve put together a closer look at <a href="/destination-wedding-in-udaipur"><strong>destination wedding venues in Udaipur</strong></a> that compares these options side by side.</p><p> </p><h2 id="what-makes-jaipur-a-strong-choice-for-a-royal-wedding">What Makes Jaipur a Strong Choice for a Royal Wedding?</h2><p>Jaipur is often the easiest city to choose when guests are flying in from overseas. With an international airport and strong road connectivity, getting everyone there is simpler, without giving up the royal palace setting Rajasthan is known for.</p><ul><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jaipur/rambagh-palace-jaipur"><strong>Rambagh Palace</strong></a>, once home to the Jaipur royal family, remains one of the most iconic luxury wedding venues in Rajasthan<strong> </strong>and India.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jaipur/fairmont-jaipur"><strong>Fairmont Jaipur</strong></a> is considered one of the <strong>best wedding venues in Rajasthan, </strong>bringing a more contemporary read on Rajputana design, with lawns and ballrooms suited to guest lists running into the hundreds.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jaipur/samode-bagh-jaipur"><strong>Samode Palace</strong></a>, just outside the city, offers heritage grandeur without the crowds of central Jaipur.</li></ul><p>A palace wedding here usually begins around INR 30 to 50 lakhs for essentials, with premium venues and full guest hospitality pushing the total well past INR 1 crore. Our team has mapped out venue-wise comparisons for a <a href="/destination-wedding-in-jaipur"><strong>destination wedding in Jaipur</strong></a> if you want to go deeper on this city specifically.</p><p> </p><h2 id="why-do-couples-pick-jodhpur-for-a-grand-destination-wedding">Why Do Couples Pick Jodhpur for a Grand Destination Wedding?</h2><p>For a destination wedding in Rajasthan that leans into scale and drama, Jodhpur is hard to beat:</p><ul><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jodhpur/umaid-bhawan-palace-jodhpur"><strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong></a><strong> </strong>rises above the Jodhpur skyline as one of the world’s largest private residences and remains one of India’s most iconic settings for grand, high-profile weddings.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jodhpur/taj-hari-mahal-jodhpur"><strong>Taj Hari Mahal in Jodhpur</strong></a><strong>, </strong>a palace-style five-star hotel rather than a heritage monument, hosts opulent receptions across its sprawling lawns and terraces overlooking the blue city below.</li><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jodhpur/indana-palace-jodhpur"><strong>Indana Palace Jodhpur</strong></a> captures the charm of a royal palace with carved façades, spacious courtyards and elegant wedding venues.</li></ul><p>Weddings at properties of this stature typically start from around INR 1 Cr, reflecting their scale and exclusivity. If you’re planning a <a href="/destination-wedding-in-jodhpur"><strong>destination wedding in Jodhpur</strong></a><strong>,</strong> we’ve compared these venues in greater detail to help you choose the right fit.</p><p> </p><h2 id="are-there-destination-wedding-venues-beyond-the-usual-cities">Are There Destination Wedding Venues Beyond the Usual Cities?</h2><p>Two properties worth considering for a destination wedding outside Rajasthan’s big three cities include:</p><ul><li><a href="/destination-wedding/jaisalmer/suryagarh-palace-jaisalmer"><strong>Suryagarh, Jaisalmer</strong></a> offers a complete desert wedding experience, with dune-side dinners, candlelit courtyards and the atmosphere of a restored fortress. Celebrations here typically start around INR 2 crore for intimate weddings and can go considerably higher for larger, multi-day events.</li><li><strong>The Leela Jaisalmer </strong>opens on 15th December, bringing signature luxury, warm hospitality and a fresh destination wedding experience to Rajasthan’s desert landscape.</li><li> </li></ul><h2 id="which-rajasthan-wedding-venue-matches-your-celebration">Which Rajasthan Wedding Venue Matches Your Celebration?</h2><p>Everyone hears about the same five or six palaces, but not every one of them suits every guest count or budget. A quick way to think about it:</p><figure class="table"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Priority</strong></td><td><strong>Best Fit</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Ultra-intimate, high privacy</td><td>Taj Lake Palace, Udaipur, Neemrana Fort Palace</td></tr><tr><td>Grand, large-scale celebration</td><td>Umaid Bhawan Palace, Rambagh Palace Jaipur</td></tr><tr><td>Balance of scale and cost</td><td>Fairmont Jaipur, The Leela Palace Udaipur</td></tr><tr><td>Unique, non-lake setting</td><td>Suryagarh Palace, Jaisalmer</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>At <a href="/"><strong>Viraaya Weddings</strong></a>, we help you compare venue availability and pricing across your shortlisted venues, making it much easier to see which one is the right fit.</p><p> </p><h2 id="how-early-should-i-start-booking-a-wedding-venue-in-rajasthan">How Early Should I Start Booking a Wedding Venue in Rajasthan?</h2><p>If you’re planning a wedding between October and March, it’s worth starting your venue search 8 to 12 months ahead. In-demand dates fill up fast, and rates typically rise as availability shrinks. Booking through Viraaya Weddings early also gives you the advantage of our negotiated rates.</p><p>Rajasthan gives you more than a backdrop. It gives you centuries of history to stand in front of. The hardest part isn’t finding a beautiful venue. It’s finding the one that suits your guest list, season and budget without months of back-and-forth with hotel sales teams. That’s the part we handle.</p><p><a href="/wedding-consultation"><strong>Book a consultation</strong> </a>to shortlist the right Rajasthan wedding venue with confidence.</p>', '[{"id": 31, "question": "What is the average cost of a luxury destination wedding in Rajasthan?", "answer": "<p>The cost of a luxury destination wedding in Rajasthan depends on the venue, guest count and scale of your celebration. Boutique weddings at heritage properties can start around INR 70 lakhs, while grand palace weddings at venues like Umaid Bhawan Palace or Rambagh Palace can exceed INR 2 to 5 Cr.</p>"}, {"id": 32, "question": "Which city in Rajasthan is best for a lakeside wedding versus a desert wedding?", "answer": "<p>The best city in Rajasthan depends on the setting you have in mind. Udaipur is the natural choice for lakeside weddings, with iconic venues around Lake Pichola, while Jaisalmer is ideal if you’re looking for desert landscapes, fort backdrops and a more distinctive setting.</p>"}, {"id": 33, "question": "How much can I save by booking a Rajasthan wedding venue through Viraaya Weddings instead of directly?", "answer": "<p>While the exact saving depends on the hotel and season, couples who book through Viraaya Weddings can often access rates that are around 10% to 15% lower, along with transparent venue comparisons and personalised guidance. Our team also compares venues, availability and pricing for you, making it easier to shortlist the right hotel with confidence.</p>"}]', 'Top 10 Destination Wedding Places in Rajasthan for Luxury Celebrations', 'Every third couple who walks into a conversation with us at Viraaya Weddings mentions Rajasthan before we even ask where they’re...', '/storage/blogs/fMkxUPVWyH9i9g0VTTX0Mdfg2NFbGNAtDBhMhPTh.webp'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `blog_posts` WHERE `slug` = 'top-destination-wedding-places-rajasthan');
--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `blog_posts` (slug, status, position, seo_title, meta_description, og_image, banner_image, category, heading, published_label, author, body_html, faqs, card_title, card_excerpt, card_image)
SELECT 'questions-to-ask-destination-wedding-planner', 'published', 2, 'Questions to Ask Before Hiring a Wedding Planner', 'Choose the perfect destination wedding planner with these 15 important questions covering budgets, vendors, timelines and coordination.', '/storage/blog/seo/b5A3LFz8sxfiOXuq5RyugrGOefBdqwpvNd3XgcJV.webp', '/storage/blogs/4BJV2h2lpHkuq2yQezmurLIyr1iMy6Mw6jbkRha8.webp', 'Wedding Planning', '15 Questions to Ask a Destination Wedding Planner Before Hiring', 'August 06, 2026', 'Viraaya Weddings Team', '<!--?xml encoding="UTF-8"--><p>After a couple says "yes" to one of the most important questions they''ll ever hear, the planning begins. Maybe you''ve already picked a city, or perhaps you''re still deciding between the convenience of an urban wedding and the charm of a more secluded destination. Either way, you''re balancing budgets, guest lists, logistics and the vision you''ve imagined for your big day. It''s a lot to think about but, dare we say, it''s also part of the fun.</p><p>After more than 10 years of planning destination weddings, we''ve learnt that the magic isn''t just in the venue or the décor. It''s in having someone who''s always thinking three steps ahead. You can benefit greatly from the reassurance of a fresh set of eyes and someone who understands the million moving parts that must come together to execute a destination wedding. </p><p>Of course, not every team is the right fit for every couple. How you figure this out is by asking the right questions to your <a href="/about-us"><strong>destination wedding planner</strong></a> (before you sign anything).</p><p>Think of this as your <strong>wedding planner checklist</strong> for the most important meeting you''ll have before the big day.</p><p> </p><h2 id="what-should-you-know-before-you-talk-to-your-wedding-planner">What Should You Know Before You Talk to Your Wedding Planner?</h2><p>Let''s give you some news straight from the horse''s mouth: your wedding planner can''t work from a vague ~feeling alone. We''ve spoken with more than 1,000 families over the years, and it’s been particularly easy to talk things out with those who arrive with some rough ideas. Here’s what we recommend you decide beforehand:</p><ul><li>Preferred dates</li><li>Guest count</li><li>Preferred locations (no rules here!) and any possible connectivity preferences (where will your family be travelling from?)</li><li>Estimated budget</li></ul><p>Remember, the more clarity you bring into the room, the more productive and meaningful the conversation becomes.</p><p>Start with the big picture and work backward. </p><p> </p><h2 id="whats-their-experience-and-track-record">What’s Their Experience and Track Record?</h2><p>Maybe this is a no brainer but here’s how to get a clear idea:</p><p><strong>1. How many destination weddings have they planned, and in which cities?</strong></p><p>A planner with strong experience in <a href="/destination-wedding-in-delhi"><strong>Delhi</strong></a> weddings may not have the ground-level vendor relationships that matter in <a href="/destination-wedding-in-udaipur"><strong>Udaipur</strong></a> or <a href="/destination-wedding-in-jaipur"><strong>Jaipur</strong></a>. Ask specifically about weddings in the destination you have chosen, and ask to see photographs or client references if possible.</p><p><strong>2. Have they worked with interfaith or multi-ceremony weddings before?</strong></p><p>If your wedding involves more than one religious ceremony, you need a planner who has coordinated this before. The logistics of running different ceremonies with different requirements need special experience.</p><p><strong>3. Can they share references from recent clients?</strong></p><p>Any reputable planner should be able to connect you with past clients who are willing to speak honestly about their experience.</p><p> </p><h2 id="how-does-their-wedding-planning-process-work">How Does Their Wedding Planning Process Work?</h2><p>This will give you a good idea about what you can expect in the months ahead.</p><p><strong>4. Will they be personally present on the wedding day, or will a team member manage it?</strong></p><p>Some planners are heavily involved in the planning phase and then hand over to a junior team member for execution. Figure out exactly who will be on the ground on your wedding day.</p><p><strong>5. How do they manage guest RSVPs and wedding communications?</strong></p><p>Destination weddings involve more than collecting RSVPs. Ask whether the planner manages guest confirmations, rooming lists, travel updates and event communications, or if these responsibilities remain with the couple and their families. A clear process can make the guest experience much smoother. </p><p><strong>6. How do they communicate with clients during the planning process?</strong></p><p>You may not be in the same location as the planner so clear and consistent communication is <i>not </i>optional. How will you get updates and who will be your point of contact? Do they have any preferred modes of communication?</p><p> </p><h2 id="what-is-their-pricing-and-does-it-match-your-budget">What is Their Pricing and Does it Match Your Budget?</h2><p>The perfect set of answers here varies across families. Everything you learn should help you plan out your financial responsibility.</p><p><strong>7. How do they charge, and what exactly is included in their fee?</strong></p><p>This is one of the most important <strong>questions to ask a wedding planner</strong>. Some planners charge a flat fee, others take a percentage of the total wedding budget and others combine both. </p><p><strong>8. How are they compensated for hotel bookings and venue recommendations?</strong></p><p>Asking this question can help couples understand whether the planner''s recommendations are driven solely by what''s best for the wedding or influenced by commissions from <a href="/hotel-listing"><strong>hotels and venues</strong></a>. A transparent planner will clearly explain how they''re compensated and whether any referral fees are involved. </p><p><strong>9. How do they handle budget overruns?</strong></p><p>Be direct: what happens when costs go higher than estimated? A good planner will have a clear process for flagging increases early and finding ways to rebalance the budget (if needed). </p><p> </p><h2 id="what-sort-of-vendors-and-venues-can-they-offer">What Sort of Vendors and Venues Can They Offer?</h2><p>One of the biggest benefits you get with a dedicated planner is access to their network (and with it, exclusive deals).</p><p><strong>10. Do they have existing relationships with hotels and venues at our chosen destination?</strong></p><p>Planners with strong hospitality relationships can often secure smoother communication and preferred rates with hotel teams.</p><p><strong>11. Do they work with a fixed list of vendors, or can you bring in your own?</strong></p><p>Some planners operate within a closed vendor ecosystem, which can limit your choices for photographers, décor teams, or caterers. Others are more flexible. </p><p><strong>12. How do they vet the vendors they recommend, and who manages vendor travel and accommodation?</strong></p><p>You should know that the people being brought into your wedding have been properly assessed, not just recommended because of an existing business arrangement. It''s also worth understanding who coordinates vendor travel and accommodation, especially for destination weddings where these logistics can affect both the budget and the event timeline. </p><p> </p><h2 id="what-will-things-look-like-on-the-wedding-day">What Will Things Look Like on the Wedding Day?</h2><p>You need to be able to easily visualise how much support you’ll have on the actual wedding day.</p><p><strong>13. What does their on-site team look like, and is their travel and accommodation included in the charges?</strong></p><p>Ask how many team members will be present throughout the celebrations, what responsibilities they''ll handle and whether their travel and accommodation are already included in the planner''s fee. It''s equally important to understand how a seasoned destination wedding planner will<strong> </strong>respond if unexpected issues arise, from bad weather to vendor delays. </p><p><strong>14. How do they manage guest logistics for a destination wedding?</strong></p><p>Ask how they’ll manage the significant operation of managing guest travel, hotel room allocations, shuttle arrangements and airport transfers.</p><p><strong>15. What is their plan if something goes wrong on the wedding day?</strong></p><p>Weather, vendor no-shows, a power failure during the reception: destination weddings are especially vulnerable to the unexpected. A seasoned destination wedding planner will have thought through these scenarios and will be able to explain how they handle them.</p><p> </p><h2 id="how-to-use-this-list-for-your-destination-wedding">How to Use This List for Your Destination Wedding</h2><p>That was a lot, but remember, you do not need to fire all fifteen <strong>questions at your destination wedding planner</strong> in your first meeting. Use the ones that feel most relevant to your situation and where you are in the planning process. </p><p>Couples who go into these meetings already knowing their destination, their guest count, preferred dates and their working budget tend to get far more out of them.</p><p>If you have not already spoken with a wedding expert to plan your dream wedding, you may want to start now. Share your wedding details with us using the form below, and our team will get in touch to understand your requirements, answer your questions and help you plan the next steps.</p><p>Our goal is simple: to make the process a little easier and far more enjoyable from the very beginning. </p><p><a href="/wedding-consultation"><strong>Book a consultation with Viraaya Weddings</strong></a></p>', '[{"id": 25, "question": "When should I start looking for a destination wedding planner in India?", "answer": "<p>For a destination wedding at a premium property in cities like Udaipur, Jaisalmer, or Goa, it is generally advisable to begin the search at least 8 to 12 months prior, especially if you are planning for the peak October to March season.</p>"}, {"id": 26, "question": "How do I know if a destination wedding planner is right for my wedding?", "answer": "<p>When searching for a destination wedding planner, look for three things: relevant experience in your chosen destination, clear and honest answers about pricing and vendor relationships, and a communication style that feels comfortable. References from recent clients are also invaluable.</p>"}, {"id": 27, "question": "What to bring to the first meeting with a wedding planner?", "answer": "<p>During your first meeting with a wedding planner, bring as many ideas as you can. You should ideally come to the first wedding with ideas about your hotel and the dates you want blocked. The rest of the meeting will be about your vision for the decor, photography, entertainment and other vendors (along with your budget breakdown for each!). It is equally important to come prepared with your non-negotiables, your nice-to-haves, and a list of things you absolutely do not want.</p>"}]', '15 Questions to Ask a Destination Wedding Planner Before Hiring', 'After a couple says &quot;yes&quot; to one of the most important questions they''ll ever hear, the planning begins. Maybe you''ve al...', '/storage/blogs/4BJV2h2lpHkuq2yQezmurLIyr1iMy6Mw6jbkRha8.webp'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `blog_posts` WHERE `slug` = 'questions-to-ask-destination-wedding-planner');
--> statement-breakpoint
INSERT INTO `blog_posts` (slug, status, position, seo_title, meta_description, og_image, banner_image, category, heading, published_label, author, body_html, faqs, card_title, card_excerpt, card_image)
SELECT 'new-luxury-wedding-hotels-in-india', 'published', 3, 'New Luxury Wedding Hotels in India Opening in 2026', 'India’s luxury wedding scene will welcome six new luxury wedding hotels from 2026 to 2028. Compare venues, accommodation and opening timelines before you book.', '/storage/blog/seo/2Gq4s0IgkP49ljFBZP9QR7jMCWD8Rp1KlJMerXeV.webp', '/storage/blogs/UxsODRx1HByqkBnQ6nfXgvsVnkl4PgbJqQVcB33S.webp', 'Wedding Planning', 'India’s Newest Luxury Wedding Hotels: A First Look at Leela Jaisalmer, Fairmont Agra & More', 'August 07, 2026', '', '<!--?xml encoding="UTF-8"--><p>If you’re planning a destination wedding over the next year or two, you have something previous couples didn’t: a whole new set of luxury hotels to choose from. Between 2026 and 2027, six new five-star properties are opening across India, including three in Rajasthan. Booking early doesn’t just give you more choice. It can also mean better availability, launch offers and room blocks before demand picks up.</p><p>At Viraaya Weddings, we track these openings the moment they’re announced, because early access is where the real savings sit. Here’s everything you need to know about the <strong>new luxury wedding hotels in India</strong> before everyone else catches on.</p><h2> </h2><h2 id="which-new-5-star-wedding-hotels-in-india-are-opening-right-now">Which New 5-Star Wedding Hotels in India Are Opening Right Now?</h2><p>With the checklist out of the way, here’s a detailed breakdown of each property, what sets it apart and what it offers for destination weddings:</p><h3> </h3><h3 id="1-the-leela-jaisalmer">1) The Leela Jaisalmer</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 80, across villas and tented suites</p><p><strong>Residential Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 160 to 240 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: Multiple restaurants and bars</p><p><strong>Opening: </strong>15th December 2026</p><p>Set across 30 acres of desert landscape near the UNESCO-listed Jaisalmer Fort, this is <i>The Leela’s</i> first entry into Jaisalmer and one of the more striking <strong>new wedding venues in Rajasthan</strong>. The resort houses a pillarless ballroom and extensive outdoor spaces for weddings and events, which makes it a strong pick if you want desert dunes in your wedding photos without sacrificing five-star service.</p><h3> </h3><h3 id="2-fairmont-agra">2) Fairmont Agra</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 205, including 44 suites</p><p><strong>Residential Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 410 to 610 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: 4 venues, a signature restaurant, speciality restaurant, coffee shop and bar</p><p><strong>Opening: </strong>Late 2026</p><p>This is the first Fairmont property in Agra, and it fills a real gap. Featuring regal architecture, built along the banks of the Yamuna, just minutes from the Taj Mahal, it brings a new tier of luxury to <a href="/destination-wedding-in-agra"><strong>destination weddings in Agra</strong></a>. Set to open in late 2026, it’s worth serious consideration for its prime location and authentic design.</p><h3> </h3><h3 id="3-mayfair-bhubaneswar">3) Mayfair, Bhubaneswar</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 100 (flagship Mayfair Lagoon property)</p><p><strong>Residential Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 200 to 300 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: 6 restaurants &amp; bars</p><p><strong>Opening: </strong>September 2026</p><p>Mayfair is expanding its footprint in Bhubaneswar, a city known for its temple architecture. The new property, opening in 2026, positions itself as one of India’s latest luxury wedding resorts for couples looking east instead of west. Its generous scale makes it a great fit for weddings with multiple functions, without having to move guests between venues.</p><h3> </h3><h3 id="4-kingsbury-lake-island-resort-udaipur">4) Kingsbury Lake Island Resort, Udaipur</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 145</p><p><strong>Residential Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 300 to 440 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: Multiple restaurants and bars</p><p><strong>Expected Opening: </strong>January 2027</p><p>Unlike most hotels that adapt existing banquet halls for weddings, Kingsbury was designed from the ground up as an event destination, with rooftop celebration spaces and water-facing views. For a mid-sized <a href="/destination-wedding-in-udaipur"><strong>wedding in Udaipur</strong></a>, this is one of the more interesting newly launched wedding venues in India to keep an eye on. </p><h3> </h3><h3 id="5-conrad-jaipur">5) Conrad Jaipur</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 246</p><p><strong>Expected Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 250 to 300 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: Multiple restaurants and bars</p><p><strong>Expected Opening: </strong>2027</p><p>This marks Hilton’s second luxury Hilton brand in Jaipur, and it’s built with weddings in mind from the start. If your timeline stretches into 2027, <strong>Conrad Jaipur by Hilton</strong> can be worth holding a placeholder date for.</p><h3> </h3><h3 id="6-grand-hyatt-jaipur">6) Grand Hyatt Jaipur</h3><p><strong>Rooms</strong>: 409, set across 21 acres</p><p><strong>Residential Guest Capacity</strong>: Approximately 800 to 1200 guests</p><p><strong>Dining</strong>: Multiple restaurants, bars and a club lounge</p><p><strong>Expected Opening</strong>: Late 2026</p><p>Grand Hyatt’s Rajasthan debut adds another internationally recognised luxury brand to Jaipur’s wedding scene. If you’re planning a destination wedding in 2026 or beyond, it’s one of the new 5-star wedding hotels in India worth watching as bookings begin.</p><h2> </h2><h2 id="why-booking-in-the-first-season-actually-works-in-your-favour">Why Booking in the First Season Actually Works in Your Favour</h2><p>Newly launched wedding venues in India offer more than just fresh spaces and Instagram-worthy photo spots. Booking early can also give you access to a few advantages that become harder to find later:</p><ul><li><strong>More flexible pricing</strong>, as many properties are still establishing themselves in the wedding market.</li><li><strong>Better date availability,</strong> giving you a wider choice of weekends and celebration dates.</li><li><strong>Greater room inventory</strong>, making it easier to accommodate larger guest lists at one property.</li><li><strong>A fresh venue,</strong> where your wedding won’t look like countless celebrations that have already taken place.</li><li><strong>Closer coordination,</strong> as newer properties often work more closely with early wedding bookings to ensure everything runs smoothly.</li></ul><h2> </h2><h2 id="quick-comparison-new-wedding-hotels-at-a-glance">Quick Comparison: New Wedding Hotels at a Glance</h2><p>Here’s a side-by-side comparison to help you shortlist the right property faster:</p><figure class="table"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Hotel</strong></td><td><strong>City</strong></td><td><strong>Rooms</strong></td><td><strong>Best For</strong></td></tr><tr><td>The Leela Jaisalmer</td><td>Jaisalmer</td><td>80</td><td>Desert weddings, dramatic photography</td></tr><tr><td>Fairmont Agra</td><td>Agra</td><td>205</td><td>Taj Mahal backdrop</td></tr><tr><td>Mayfair, Bhubaneswar</td><td>Bhubaneswar</td><td>100</td><td>Multi-function weddings, eastern India</td></tr><tr><td>Kingsbury Lake Island Resort</td><td>Udaipur</td><td>145</td><td>Mid-sized lakeside weddings</td></tr><tr><td>Conrad Jaipur by Hilton</td><td>Jaipur</td><td>246</td><td>Global brand standard</td></tr><tr><td>Grand Hyatt Jaipur</td><td>Jaipur</td><td>409</td><td>Large-scale, multi-day celebrations</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h2> </h2><h2 id="secure-your-venue-with-viraayaweddings">Secure Your Venue With Viraaya Weddings</h2><p>Launch pricing on new luxury wedding hotels in India rarely stays flexible for long. Once a property gets its first few high-profile weddings, rates climb. Our team at <a href="/"><strong>Viraaya Weddings</strong></a> will help you secure availability across all six of these hotels as bookings open, negotiate through our existing partnerships and give you a transparent, itemised price breakdown before you commit to anything. That’s the difference between chasing a new hotel and actually booking it at the right price.</p><p><a href="/wedding-consultation"><strong>Get in touch with our team</strong></a> to compare these new luxury wedding hotels, check availability and find the right fit for your celebration.</p>', '[{"id": 22, "question": "Are these new luxury wedding hotels in India ready to take bookings today?", "answer": "<p>Some of these new luxury wedding hotels in India are already accepting enquiries and advance bookings, while others are still gearing up for launch. We keep a close eye on opening timelines and let couples know the right time to secure their preferred venue.</p>"}, {"id": 23, "question": "Is it riskier to book a wedding at a newly opened hotel?", "answer": "<p>Not necessarily. While newly opened hotels have fewer weddings to showcase, most of these properties are backed by well-established hospitality brands or experienced developers. At Viraaya Weddings, we also verify venue readiness before recommending any property to our couples.</p>"}, {"id": 24, "question": "Can Viraaya Weddings compare these new hotels against established venues in the same city?", "answer": "<p>Yes. Viraaya Weddings compares new hotels with established wedding venues on cost, guest capacity, event spaces and overall suitability, helping you make a well-informed decision.</p>"}]', 'India’s Newest Luxury Wedding Hotels: A First Look at Leela Jaisalmer, Fairmont Agra & More', 'If you’re planning a destination wedding over the next year or two, you have something previous couples didn’t: a whole...', '/storage/blogs/UxsODRx1HByqkBnQ6nfXgvsVnkl4PgbJqQVcB33S.webp'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `blog_posts` WHERE `slug` = 'new-luxury-wedding-hotels-in-india');
